      "message": "The Combine Lists line breaks the Skip logic — test will always be skipped.\n\n@{ipv4_addressorigin_list} is already a flat list like [\u0027Static\u0027, \u0027IPv4LinkLocal\u0027]. Using @{...} here unpacks each string as a separate argument to Combine Lists, which then iterates over each string\u0027s characters instead of treating them as whole values — turning the list into individual letters ([\u0027S\u0027, \u0027t\u0027, \u0027a\u0027, \u0027t\u0027, \u0027i\u0027, \u0027c\u0027, \u0027I\u0027, \u0027P\u0027, \u0027v\u0027, \u00274\u0027, ...]).\n\nAs a result, \u0027Static\u0027 not in $ipv4_addressorigin_list is always True (no single letter equals \u0027Static\u0027), so the test always gets skipped. Same problem affects the \u0027DHCP\u0027.\n\nso remove the line ${ipv4_addressorigin_list}\u003d  Combine Lists  @{ipv4_addressorigin_list}",
      "revId": "f8a8126437419560235cb2b0485437b8090b2279",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
