      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your review. I had run the test for both with eth1 having static ip and not having a static IP and the results were as intended. The Combine Lists line is actually needed here and mirrors the same pattern used in \u0027Verify Static IPv4 Functionality\u0027 in lib/bmc_ipv6_utils.robot.\n\nWhen Get Address Origin List And IPv4 or IPv6 Address returns two scalars and they are assigned to @{ipv4_addressorigin_list} ${ipv4_addr_list}, Robot wraps the first return value into a list-of-list  [[\u0027Static\u0027]]. Combine Lists then flattens it back to [\u0027Static\u0027], which is what we need for the Skip If check.\n\nRemoving it would actually cause the opposite problem \u0027Static\u0027 not in [[\u0027Static\u0027]] is always True, so the test would always skip.\n\nThis is also confirmed by the output.xml log which shows @{ipv4_addressorigin_list} \u003d [ [] ] before Combine Lists and [\u0027Static\u0027] after.",
